# Configuration for slurm/train_gan.sh 256, read when the job starts.
#
# The same configuration as gan128.args - the only one of four in
# slurm/sweep_gan.sh that did not collapse (see that file for the numbers).
#
# Steps: a 128x128 run with an R1 penalty took 1 h 44 min for 40,000 steps
# (job 591010), about 155 ms a step against 97 ms without R1. The smoke test
# measured 188 ms at 256x256 without R1, so about 300 ms is expected with it,
# and 30,000 steps (about 100 passes over the data at batch 32) fit one job's
# 170 minutes. If they do not, resubmitting resumes.
--steps 30000
--loss logistic
--r1-gamma 10
--no-spectral-norm
--diffaugment=
--lr-g 2e-4
--lr-d 2e-4
--beta2 0.99
